What is a Bidirectional DC Charger?
A Bidirectional DC Charger is an advanced type of electric vehicle (EV) charging equipment that supports the two-way flow of energy between an EV's battery and the power grid. This technology enables the charger to not only supply electricity to the vehicle (Grid-to-Vehicle or G2V) but also to draw energy from the vehicle's battery and feed it back into the grid (Vehicle-to-Grid or V2G). The core of this system lies in its sophisticated bidirectional power conversion technology, which allows it to function as both a charger and a distributed energy resource, effectively transforming EVs into mobile energy storage units capable of supporting grid stability.
